# Godot 4 editor data
.godot/
*.translation

# Editor/OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
export_presets.cfg

# Godot import metadata: regenerated per machine, and a guaranteed pull conflict when the
# project is opened on both a PC and an iPad. The height maps and screenshots are data, not
# textures - the .gdignore files next to them keep Godot from importing them at all.
*.import

# ...except the two that carry settings which exist NOWHERE ELSE. A rigged model's scale has
# to be nodes/root_scale, because scaling above a Skeleton3D breaks skinning - so ignoring
# these meant a fresh clone regenerated them with defaults and got a captain at 53% height
# with a broken jump. Two files, so the conflict surface stays tiny; tests/import_check.gd
# fails if either is ever lost again.
!art/models/captain.glb.import
!art/models/grunt.glb.import
